oiding the least vertex of a symmetric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"difference. Every vertex with a self-loop is in it; parallel edges count once. The cost is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":"’s: O(m √n) on bipartite components."}]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/isEdgeCover(_:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isEdgeCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether every vertex is an end of some edge in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" (positions). Repeats are ignored."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(n + m)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isEdgeCover(_:)","title":"isEdgeCover(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isedgecover(_:)"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"bipartition","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bipartition","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15BipartiteGraphs11BipartitionV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"König’s minimum vertex cover of a bipartite graph: from a maximum matching (Hopcroft–Karp on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the sides), Z is the set of vertices reached from the free left vertices by alternating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths, an edge not in the matching from left to right, then the matched edge back; the cover","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"is (left ∖ Z) ∪ (right ∩ Z), in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order. It is the one minimum cover with the most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left vertices, so it does not depend on the matching. O(m √n)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)","title":"minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumvertexcover(bipartition:)"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximalIndependentSet(containing:)":{"title":"maximalIndependentSet(containing:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalIndependentSet(containing:)","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalindependentset(containing:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A maximal independent set containing ","type":"text"},{"code":"seeds","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which go in first, then each vertex in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order as ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximalIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; nil when ","type":"text"},{"code":"seeds","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is not an independent set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(two are adjacent, or one has a self-loop). Repeats are one seed. O(n + m).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximalIndependentSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"containing","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST","text":"Sequence","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/approximateMinimumVertexCover()":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"approximateMinimumVertexCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/approximateMinimumVertexCover()","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/approximateminimumvertexcover()","kind":"symbol","title":"approximateMinimumVertexCover()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The same with every weight 1. On a graph without self-loops it lies within the ends of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximalMatching()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumIndependentSet()":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumIndependentSet"},{"kind":"text","tex